d to practice law as an attorney-at-law, solicitor, advocate, barrister or equivalent, i.e. represent parties in lawsuits or trials and give legal advice.", "tags": [], "examples": ["A lawyer's time and advice are his stock in trade. [one of various versions of an aphorism in law]"], "quotes": [{"text": "His forefathers had been, as a rule, professional men—physicians and lawyers; his grandfather died under the walls of Chapultepec Castle while twisting a tourniquet for a cursing dragoon; an uncle remained indefinitely at Malvern Hill;[…].", "reference": "1907 August, Robert W[illiam] Chambers, chapter II, in The Younger Set, New York, N.Y.: D. Appleton & Company, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "Mr. Wells was a pleasant man of middle-age, with keen eyes, and the typical lawyer’s mouth.", "reference": "1920, Agatha Christie, The Mysterious Affair at Styles, London: Pan Books, published 1954, page 59:"}], "synonyms": ["advocate", "attorney", "counselor"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "ügyvéd"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(by extension) A legal layman who argues points of law.", "tags": ["broadly"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "(juridisch) raadsman"}, {"language": {"code": "it", "name": "Italian"}, "word": "giurista"}, {"language": {"code": "la", "name": "Latin"}, "word": "iurisconsultus"}, {"language": {"code": "scn", "name": "Sicilian"}, "word": "jurista"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "leguleyo"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "abogado de secano"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "tinterillo"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "rábula"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(UK, colloquial) The burbot.", "tags": ["UK", "colloquial"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(UK, dialect) The stem of a bramble.", "tags": ["UK", "dialectal"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Any of various plants that have hooked thorns.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": [{"definition": "A relative of the raspberry found in Australia and New Zealand, Rubus australis", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The species of Eugnomus are very partial to the lawyer (Rubus australis ) when in bloom.", "reference": "1881 April, George M. Thomson, “On the Fertilization of New Zealand Flowering Plants”, in Transactions and Proceedings of the New Zealand Institute, volume 13, page 250:"}, {"text": "In the lawyer (Rubus australis) a considerable differentiation has taken place. All the alllies of this plant (such as the true roses, brambles, rasps, &c.), exhibit a strong development of epidermal structures in the form of hooks, spines, or hairs, but in none are these structures so perfect as in our lawyer.", "reference": "1885, New Zealand Journal of Science - Volume 2, page 417:"}, {"text": "A plant that is excessively troublesome in the localities where the native vegetation has been least disturbed is the “lawyer” (Rubus australis).", "reference": "1915, John Henderson, P. Marshall, Percy Gates Morgan, The Geology and Mineral Resources of the Reefton Subdivision, Westport and North Westland Division, page 6:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Various species of Calamus, including Calamus australis, Calamus muelleri, Calamus obstruens, Calamus vitiensis, Calamus warburgii, and Calamus moti.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Besides the bags and nets common throughout the continent, these tribes have water-bags, which they make of closely-plaited “lawyer” (Calamus Australis), and also of palm-leaf sewn with the sinews of animals.", "reference": "1886, Edward Micklethwaite Curr, The Australian Race, page 427:"}, {"text": "The nest was a foot or two from the ground, and placed in a bunch of lawyer (Calamus ) canes.", "reference": "1901, Archibald James Campbell, Nests and Eggs of Australian Birds, page 267:"}, {"text": "This lawyer (Calamus australis) is a climbing palm, throwing up shoots from its roots as thick as a man's finger and tough as wire, covered with sharp spines, and bearing much divided leaves, alternating with tendrils twenty feel long.", "reference": "1905, W. J. Gordon, “Jackey Jackey”, in The Boy's Own Annual, volume 28, page 318:"}, {"text": "They were usually very neatly laid out under arching masses of the exasperating lawyer-palm vines ( Calamus moti and C. australis ), and consequently not too easy to examine.", "reference": "1910 October, Sidney Wm. Jackson, “Additional Notes on Tooth-billed Bower-Bird (Scenopaeetes dentirostris) of North Queensland”, in The Emu: Official Organ of the Australasian Ornithologists' Union, volume 10, page 84:"}, {"text": "Lawyer Vine (Calamus muelleri), also known as Hairy Mary and Wait-a-while, is actually a palm, that grows in long canes that loop and snake through the undergrowth.", "reference": "2014, Germaine Greer, White Beech: The Rainforest Years, page 171:"}, {"text": "The trail of the lawyer vine (CALAMUS OBSTRUENS), with its leaf sheath and long tentacles bristling with incurved hooks, is over it all.", "reference": "2022, E. J. Banfield, The Confessions of a Beachcomber:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A woody climbing rainforest vine, Flagellaria indica.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The stems of the \"lawyer vine\" (Flagellaria indica), buz or buzi (W.), boz (E.), are used in house-building, tying fences, etc.", "reference": "2011, A. C. Haddon, W. H. R. Rivers, Reports of the Cambridge Anthropological Expedition to Torres Straits, page 89:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}]}], "synonyms": ["abogado", "advocate", "attorney", "avocat", "counsel", "counselor", "latitat", "lawman", "lawyer", "legal representative", "limb of the law", "man of law"], "antonyms": ["non-lawyer"]}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlɔːjə(ɹ)/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlɔɪ.ə(ɹ)/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlɔɪ.ɚ/", "tags": ["Northern", "US", "Western"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlɔ.jɚ/", "tags": ["Southern", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlɔɪ.əɹ/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlɔɪ.ɐ/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlɔjə(ɾ)/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlɑjə(ɾ)/", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "lawyers", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "lawyering", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "lawyered", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "lawyered", "tags": ["past"]}, {"word": "lawer", "tags": ["alternative", "obsolete"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(informal, intransitive) To practice law.", "tags": ["informal", "intransitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "adwokatować"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(intransitive) To perform, or attempt to perform, the work of a lawyer.", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(intransitive) To make legalistic arguments.", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(informal, transitive) To barrage (a person) with questions in order to get them to admit something.", "tags": ["informal", "transitive"], "examples": ["You've been lawyered!"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawyer", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}